{"agent":"main-red","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change replaces the call-time `from . import install_kind as _install_kind` with a direct call to `install_kind()`. That deleted indirection was not redundant: it made `upgrade_remedy` resolve `ddflow.infra.log.install_kind` from the package at call time, so tests or callers that monkeypatch `ddflow.infra.log.install_kind` are observed. For example, with `import ddflow.infra.log as log; log.install_kind = lambda: \"source\"; log.upgrade_remedy(\"1.0.0\")`, the old code used the patched `\"source\"`; the new code calls the module-local `_skew.install_kind` and emits advice for the real install kind, which is the exact pre-split behavior the removed comment says was a bug.","digest":"cbbbbf273d449bdf","location":"ddflow/infra/log/_skew.py:41 upgrade_remedy","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/infra/log/_skew.py:41 upgrade_remedy"},{"chunk":1,"detail":"This renamed file remains a direct manipulation of process environment (`os.environ`) rather than going through a port in `ddflow/adapters`, violating [r-adapters], which explicitly lists `environment` as an external dependency that must be adapted. Calling `ddflow.infra.threads.cap_blas_threads()` mutates `os.environ` in-process with no adapter seam, so a fake cannot intercept it and the change simply moves the non-compliant code into `infra` instead of fixing the seam.","digest":"a49637124edebde5","location":"ddflow/infra/threads.py cap_blas_threads","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/infra/threads.py cap_blas_threads"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The rename moves `ddflow/_threads.py` to `ddflow/infra/threads.py` with no content change (`+0 -0`), so the direct `os.environ` write in that file remains. This violates [r-adapters]: environment access is an external dependency and must go through a port in `ddflow/adapters`. The move fixes the layering location but does not address the unported environment dependency.","digest":"5942706724a5b5df","location":"ddflow/infra/threads.py","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/infra/threads.py"}],"chunks_total":2,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":7127,"diff_sha":"46abb586d1f178bc8e717698147b3bcabea24ed733ff00779af4e4715fe4ea63","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":173.0,"family":"deepseek","findings":3,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813-Godzila","output_digest":"81ad86856ba15038","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-main-red-layering-threads-and-cycles.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4-pro.20261104T234929Z-ebb529e1.jsonl","reason":"","review_id":"0ae98894545e","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"6bf7d015dec57347efd1df17e68959b69003f6fc","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/_threads.py":"","ddflow/api/knowledge/self_assessment.py":"100644 14fed27942571174ea36c152dfa7dee1a07ce68f","ddflow/infra/log/_skew.py":"100644 277008f894d253bc9baf2a9d37bf8e71b010e9f9","ddflow/infra/threads.py":"100644 93e40d9d0ab8377c3a0e85e33d84a7f4542cba04","ddflow/surfaces/cli.py":"100644 c9839d453e5dd9780034a6ad2d9a38aff679fbc2","ddflow/surfaces/mcp/_serve.py":"100644 3cf6f256bf31020fe77deb27de62903e88203f5a","tests/test_no_eager_embed.py":"100644 0bf7a4cf0d12c69ab5495e8b89a5aedbdc00b827","tests/test_skew_wording.py":"100644 154b3fc5dcc5bd6729055e713d4343c1752ee7c7","tests/test_upgrade_stamp.py":"100644 3fa18d265e5e2a14cb1d366268db725b7e8c9a47"},"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4-pro","reviewer_digest":"dd08c1466c2b8632","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/infra/log/_skew.py:41 upgrade_remedy","ddflow/infra/threads.py cap_blas_threads","ddflow/infra/threads.py"],"tree_sha":"6bf7d015dec5+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"3 finding(s)"},"id":"ef8f8a9879d823a6b36a8e90b","kind":"gate.fa